This patch is needed because Solaris ld is stricter about static archive
resolution order than the GNU Linux linkers Chromium normally targets.

What it does:
- strips unsupported GNU style linker flags on Solaris
- moves Rust sysroot .rlib inputs into the trailing Rust archive group
- duplicates Rust owned .a archives discovered in response files into that
  trailing Rust group as well
- appends -lssp -lssp_nonshared

Why it is needed:
- without it, mksnapshot fails near the end of the V8 build with unresolved
  Rust runtime and allocator symbols on Solaris
